dtksh, dtappbuilder and ttsnoop optional.

Three programs cannot be built where the build machine is not the target:
- dtksh embeds CDE's ksh93, which AST's own build system (bin/package)
  makes by compiling and running hundreds of feature probes on the build
  machine;
- dtappbuilder and ttsnoop have their user interface code written at build
  time by dtcodegen, a program built in the same tree for the target.
configure.ac gets --disable-dtksh and --disable-dtappbuilder (the latter
covers ttsnoop); both default to enabled. programs/Makefile.am builds each
only when enabled, and the C locale's catalogues (dtksh, dtbuilder,
dtcodegen), app-defaults (Dtbuilder) and action types (dtbuilder.dt) are
made only with their programs. With both enabled nothing changes but the
order: the three are made after the other programs.

--- a/configure.ac	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/configure.ac	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -252,6 +252,20 @@
 AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_DTINFO], [test "x$enable_dtinfo" = xyes])
 AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_DTDOCBOOK], [test "x$enable_dtdocbook" = xyes])
 AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_MMDB], [test "x$enable_dtinfo" = xyes || test "x$enable_dtdocbook" = xyes])
+
+dnl dtksh: its ksh93 is built by AST's own build system, which runs its
+dnl feature probes on the build host
+AC_ARG_ENABLE([dtksh],
+        AS_HELP_STRING([--disable-dtksh], [Do not build dtksh (default=build it)]),
+        [], [enable_dtksh=yes])
+AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_DTKSH], [test "x$enable_dtksh" = xyes])
+
+dnl dtappbuilder and ttsnoop: dtcodegen, built in the same tree, writes
+dnl their user interface code at build time
+AC_ARG_ENABLE([dtappbuilder],
+        AS_HELP_STRING([--disable-dtappbuilder], [Do not build dtappbuilder and ttsnoop (default=build them)]),
+        [], [enable_dtappbuilder=yes])
+AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_DTAPPBUILDER], [test "x$enable_dtappbuilder" = xyes])
 
 dnl Xrender usage
 AC_ARG_ENABLE([xrender],
